{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-f54fd97c-8e1f-4d28-be50-8771b6b3f6bf","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-92834a236d551c89","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9006-a0nyhca4/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9006-decomposition.md","content":"# Decomposition Summary — RHAISTRAT-9006 (Feature Store as a supported RHOAI component)\n\nThe strategy brings Feast in as a supported, installable RHOAI component. The\nFeature Store is a **new component**: it has a reserved Jira component but no\narchitecture context file, no productized repository, no build pipeline, and no\noperator integration — so it gets the full new-component onboarding chain\n(Rule 20). The strategy's single open question (deployment topology:\noperator-based vs. standalone server per project) is a genuine unknown with two\nbounded outcomes that changes what the productization epic does and how the\nPlatform Operator integration approaches enablement — it is modeled as a gating\nInvestigation with conditional decomposition branches.\n\nThe strategy contains no Staff Engineer Input section; no overrides to log.\n\n## Epic List\n\n| ID | Title | Type | Team | Priority |\n|----|-------|------|------|----------|\n| RHAISTRAT-9006-E001 | Select the Feast deployment topology to productize first | Investigation | RHOAI Feature Store | P0 |\n| RHAISTRAT-9006-E002 | Create the midstream Feast repository under opendatahub-io | Implementation (repo-onboarding) | RHOAI Feature Store | P0 |\n| RHAISTRAT-9006-E003 | License validation for Feast and its transitive dependencies | Implementation (license-validation) | RHOAI Feature Store | P0 |\n| RHAISTRAT-9006-E004 | Onboard the Feast repository to Konflux | Implementation (konflux-onboarding) | RHOAI Feature Store | P0 |\n| RHAISTRAT-9006-E005 | Enable the Feature Store as a managed component in the Platform Operator | Implementation | RHOAI Platform Operator | P0 |\n| RHAISTRAT-9006-E006 | Surface the Feature Store in the Dashboard | Implementation | RHOAI Dashboard | P1 |\n| RHAISTRAT-9006-E007 | Preinstall the Feast SDK in a supported workbench image | Implementation | RHOAI Notebooks | P1 |\n| RHAISTRAT-9006-E008 | Document Feature Store enablement, getting started, and supported limits | Implementation (docs-authoring) | RHOAI Documentation | P1 |\n| RHAISTRAT-9006-BRANCH-A-E009 | Productize the operator-based Feast deployment | Implementation (branch A) | RHOAI Feature Store | P0 |\n| RHAISTRAT-9006-BRANCH-B-E009 | Productize the standalone per-project Feast server | Implementation (branch B) | RHOAI Feature Store | P0 |\n\n`epic_count=8` counts main-plan epics; the two branch epics are conditional\nalternatives of the same unit of work (only one ships) and are attached to the\ngating Investigation as a plan document, not created as standalone issues.\n\n## Dependency DAG\n\nArrows point from dependency to dependent (\"A --> B\" = A must complete before\nB starts). Branch epics are dashed: exactly one of them activates, depending on\nthe Investigation outcome.\n\n```mermaid\ngraph TD\n    E001[\"E001 Investigation: Feast deployment topology\"] --> E005[\"E005 Platform Operator enablement\"]\n    E002[\"E002 repo-onboarding: midstream Feast repo\"] --> E004[\"E004 Konflux onboarding\"]\n    E003[\"E003 license-validation\"] --> E005\n    E003 --> E007[\"E007 Workbench image with Feast SDK\"]\n    E005 --> E006[\"E006 Dashboard integration\"]\n    E002 --> E008[\"E008 Documentation (docs-authoring)\"]\n    E003 --> E008\n    E004 --> E008\n    E005 --> E008\n    E006 --> E008\n    E007 --> E008\n    E001 -.-> BA[\"BRANCH-A-E009 operator-based productization\"]\n    E001 -.-> BB[\"BRANCH-B-E009 standalone-server productization\"]\n    E002 -.-> BA\n    E002 -.-> BB\n    E003 -.-> BA\n    E003 -.-> BB\n```\n\n## DAG Justification\n\n| Edge | Rule | Rationale |\n|------|------|-----------|\n| E002 → E004 | Rule 5 | `repo-onboarding` → `konflux-onboarding` always serial: the pipeline needs the repo to exist. |\n| E002 → BRANCH-A/B-E009 | Rule 6 | General implementation of the onboarded component needs the repo; does not block other repos (E005, E006, E007). |\n| E003 → BRANCH-A/B-E009 | Rule 9 | `license-validation` → general implementation serial: a license failure in the Feast dependency tree changes what can be productized. |\n| E003 → E005 | Rule 9 | The operator enablement ships/deploys Feast artifacts; a license failure changes the approach. |\n| E003 → E007 | Rule 9 | Shipping the Feast SDK inside a supported workbench image is gated on license clearance of its transitive deps. |\n| E001 → E005 | Rule 3 | The topology decision rewrites the operator integration approach (enable a Feast operator vs. deploy a per-project server). True gate: `gate_failure_impact.action=rewrite`. |\n| E001 → BRANCH-A/B-E009 | Rule 3 | The topology decision selects which productization branch exists. True gate: `action=remove` for the non-selected branch. |\n| E005 → E006 | Rule 13 | The Dashboard consumes the enablement state / CRs that the Platform Operator integration produces (Dashboard reads CRs; it owns no data plane). |\n| E002/E003/E004/E005/E006/E007 → E008 | Rule 11 | `docs-authoring` blocked by ALL Implementation epics — docs describe what was built. These edges do not trigger priority inheritance (docs-authoring priority exception). |\n| (no edge) E004 → E005 / BRANCH epics | Rule 10 | `konflux-onboarding` ∥ general implementation parallel by design; coupling is enforced by the \"build pipeline green\" AC on the implementation epics, never by a DAG edge. |\n| (no edge) E001 ∥ E002/E003/E004 | — | The topology investigation runs in parallel with the onboarding chain; repo creation, license scanning, and pipeline onboarding are identical under both outcomes. |\n| (no edge) E007 ∥ E001/E005 | — | Preinstalling the Feast SDK in a workbench image is topology-independent (same SDK either way) — runs in parallel. |\n\n## HLR Traceability Matrix\n\n| HLR | Priority | Requirement (abridged) | Epics |\n|-----|----------|------------------------|-------|\n| HLR-1 | P0 | Administrators can enable a supported Feature Store through the Platform Operator with productized images | E002, E003, E004, E005, BRANCH-A-E009 / BRANCH-B-E009 (exactly one) |\n| HLR-2 | P1 | Feast SDK preinstalled in at least one supported workbench image | E007 |\n| HLR-3 | P1 | Dashboard shows the Feature Store as enabled and links to its endpoints per project | E006 |\n| HLR-4 | P2 | Documentation covers enablement, getting-started, supported limits | E008 |\n\nFull coverage: every HLR maps to at least one epic; no orphaned requirements.\nPriority inheritance: E001–E005 (and both branch epics) all transitively enable\nthe P0 HLR-1 and are P0. E008 is P1 via the docs-authoring priority exception\n(strategy frontmatter `priority: Major` → P1), not via inheritance from HLR-4\n(P2).\n\n## Conditional Decomposition (bounded outcomes)\n\nThe topology open question has exactly two bounded outcomes. The productization\nunit of work differs materially between them (operator image + CRDs vs.\nper-project server image), so it is expressed as two branch epics gated by\nInvestigation E001:\n\n- **Branch A** (`RHAISTRAT-9006-BRANCH-A-E009`): operator-based deployment —\n  productize the Feast operator and its CRs. `gate_failure_impact.action=remove`\n  if the operator-based topology is not selected.\n- **Branch B** (`RHAISTRAT-9006-BRANCH-B-E009`): standalone server per project —\n  productize the Feast server image and per-project deployment.\n  `gate_failure_impact.action=remove` if the standalone topology is not selected.\n\nBoth branches share the same dependencies (the Investigation, repo-onboarding,\nlicense-validation) and remain parallel with Konflux onboarding (Rule 10).\nE005 (Platform Operator integration) stays in the main plan because HLR-1\nrequires it under either outcome — only its approach changes (`rewrite`).\n\n## Tiered Delivery\n\nNot applicable — there is no external dependency with uncertain timing. All\ngating is internal (Investigation E001) or procedural (license validation).\n\n## Component Mapping Notes\n\n- All epic `component` values are copied verbatim from\n  `.context/rhai-components.txt`: Feature Store, Platform Operator, Dashboard,\n  Notebooks, Documentation.\n- **Notebooks** is not listed in the strategy's Affected Components, but HLR-2\n  requires Feast SDK preinstallation in a supported workbench image — that is\n  Notebooks-component work, so the epic is assigned to `Notebooks` (see Health\n  Warnings).\n- The Feature Store epic set spans the strategy components \"Feature Store\"\n  (onboarding chain + productization branches); each epic keeps the single most\n  relevant canonical name.\n\n## Health Warnings\n\n1. **Missing strategy sections.** The strategy has no Impacted Teams table, no\n   Dependencies table, no Given/When/Then acceptance criteria, and no\n   Non-Functional Requirements; the Affected Components section is a bare list\n   without change/owner columns. Team assignments above follow the RHOAI\n   convention (architecture context names \"RHOAI Dashboard\" as the Dashboard\n   owning team) and must be verified with the owning teams.\n2. **Affected Components list is incomplete.** HLR-2 (workbench image with\n   Feast SDK) implies Notebooks-component work that the Affected Components\n   list omits; an epic was created for it.\n3. **Sparse architecture context.** Only Dashboard has an architecture context\n   file. Feature Store is correctly treated as new (onboarding chain per\n   Rule 20). Platform Operator, Notebooks, and Documentation lack context files\n   but are existing platform components per the strategy text (\"like any other\n   managed component\"), so no onboarding chains were generated for them.\n4. **Docs priority vs. HLR priority.** E008 is P1 (docs-authoring except