{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-924b4276295c3259","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9006-E001\n3\ttitle: Select the Feast deployment topology to productize first\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9006\n5\tcomponent: Feature Store\n6\tteam: RHOAI Feature Store\n7\ttype: Investigation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies: []\n10\tinvestigation_signals:\n11\t  question_specificity: 1\n12\t  source_accessibility: 1\n13\t  local_runnability: 1\n14\t  cluster_hardware_dependence: -1\n15\t  human_judgment_required: -1\n16\timplementation_type: null\n17\tai_signals: null\n18\tai_implementability: Medium\n19\tai_implementability_score: 1\n20\tjira_key: null\n21\tbranch: null\n22\tgated_by: null\n23\tgate_failure_impact: null\n24\t---\n25\t# Select the Feast deployment topology to productize first\n26\t\n27\t## Description\n28\t\n29\tResolves the strategy's open question: whether the supported Feature Store\n30\t(Feast) is productized as the operator-based deployment or as the standalone\n31\tserver per project. Upstream Feast supports both topologies, but their\n32\tsupportability within the platform differs (upgrade path, multi-project\n33\ttenancy, per-project endpoint model, support surface). The answer determines\n34\twhich productization work exists and how the Platform Operator enablement\n35\tintegration is approached, so this investigation runs first and gates those\n36\tdownstream epics. It does not gate the repository, license, or build-pipeline\n37\tonboarding, which are identical under both outcomes.\n38\t\n39\t## Scope\n40\t\n41\t- Evaluate both candidate topologies (operator-based deployment; standalone\n42\t  server per project) against supportability criteria: upgrade path,\n43\t  multi-project tenancy, endpoint model per project, operational support\n44\t  surface, and alignment with how the Platform Operator enables other managed\n45\t  components.\n46\t- Assess upstream maturity of each topology from upstream Feast sources\n47\t  (operator and server deployment paths).\n48\t- Produce a decision record naming the selected topology, the rationale, and\n49\t  the consequences for the Feature Store productization and the Platform\n50\t  Operator enablement integration.\n51\t- Update the conditional productization plan so the implementing team knows\n52\t  which branch applies.\n53\t\n54\t## Acceptance Criteria\n55\t\n56\t- Both candidate topologies are documented with their supportability\n57\t  trade-offs, sourced from upstream Feast material.\n58\t- A decision record exists that names the selected topology and the rationale.\n59\t- The downstream productization scope is determinate from the decision record:\n60\t  it unambiguously indicates which conditional productization approach applies.\n61\t- The support implications (what Red Hat supports under the selected topology)\n62\t  are stated in the decision record.\n63\t\n64\t## HLR Traceability\n65\t\n66\t- Enables **HLR-1** (P0): administrators can enable a supported Feature Store\n67\t  through the Platform Operator — the topology choice is a prerequisite for the\n68\t  productization and operator enablement work that delivers HLR-1.\n69\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-84770da2226bea01","agent_id":"afa180ea5d2d1d026","session_id":"ca8f2d08-a517-4b91-9d11-cd8562c17ecd","uuid":"c87f710a-1bc5-4f33-aa06-a2359c72ab4c","timestamp":"2026-10-22T17:50:08.164Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-924b4276295c3259","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9006 decomposition"}
