h upstream\n53\t  Feast source imported.\n54\t- Repository conventions (branching, permissions, metadata) match those of the\n55\t  other midstream component repositories.\n56\t- The README documents the upstream sync/patch strategy.\n57\t- The repository is buildable from a clean clone (source imports and builds\n58\t  without out-of-band steps).\n59\t\n60\t## HLR Traceability\n61\t\n62\t- **HLR-1** (P0): the productized repository is the foundation for the\n63\t  productized images and deployment that administrators enable through the\n64\t  Platform Operator.\n65\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-84770da2226bea01","agent_id":"afa180ea5d2d1d026","session_id":"ca8f2d08-a517-4b91-9d11-cd8562c17ecd","uuid":"341e4fce-5f6d-4411-9438-1c92e161b1f4","timestamp":"2026-10-22T17:50:09.014Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-9ce4b50683d41bb7","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9006 decomposition"}
