{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8fdb0c1eb317d247","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9006-E003\n3\ttitle: License validation for Feast and its transitive dependencies\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9006\n5\tcomponent: Feature Store\n6\tteam: RHOAI Feature Store\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies: []\n10\timplementation_type: license-validation\n11\tai_signals:\n12\t  change_specificity: 1\n13\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n14\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n15\t  existing_foundation: 1\n16\t  open_questions: 1\n17\t  external_dependency: 0\n18\t  human_process_gates: -1\n19\t  repo_access: 1\n20\t  architecture_claims: 0\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 4\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# License validation for Feast and its transitive dependencies\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tFeast and its Python SDK carry a large transitive dependency tree. Both the\n34\tproductized Feature Store deployment and the preinstallation of the Feast SDK\n35\tin a supported workbench image must be license-cleared before the general\n36\timplementation work locks in dependencies. This validation runs in parallel\n37\twith repository onboarding (independent inputs) and gates the general\n38\timplementation epics that depend on Feast artifacts.\n39\t\n40\t## Scope\n41\t\n42\t- Run license scanning over the Feast deployment artifacts and the Feast SDK\n43\t  dependency trees.\n44\t- Produce a report of flagged licenses with a disposition for each (approved,\n45\t  or remediation required).\n46\t- Record a go/no-go statement for productizing Feast and for shipping the\n47\t  Feast SDK inside a supported workbench image.\n48\t- Where remediation is required, record the remediation plan (dependency\n49\t  substitution, upstream patch, or scope change).\n50\t\n51\t## Acceptance Criteria\n52\t\n53\t- A license scan report exists covering Feast and its transitive dependencies\n54\t  for both the deployment and the SDK surfaces.\n55\t- Every flagged license has a recorded disposition.\n56\t- A go/no-go statement exists for productizing Feast and for including the\n57\t  Feast SDK in a supported workbench image; if no-go, a remediation plan is\n58\t  recorded.\n59\t\n60\t## HLR Traceability\n61\t\n62\t- **HLR-1** (P0): productized images may only ship license-cleared\n63\t  dependencies.\n64\t- **HLR-2** (P1): the Feast SDK may only be preinstalled in a supported\n65\t  workbench image if its dependency tree is license-cleared.\n66\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-84770da2226bea01","agent_id":"afa180ea5d2d1d026","session_id":"ca8f2d08-a517-4b91-9d11-cd8562c17ecd","uuid":"7188cfea-334e-4238-9696-a3056eb59cf6","timestamp":"2026-10-22T17:50:09.895Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-8fdb0c1eb317d247","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9006 decomposition"}
